id: stardust-barrier
name: Stardust Barrier
uaType: technical
prerequisite: Insight Score of 4+, Force Score of 8+
tpCost: 15
type: counter
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerBaseTier: 2
# Answered from Respond, as Judo Toss is: "If you are targeted by an Opponent's Energy or Magic Attack, you may use your
# Physical or Energy Strike Roll instead of your Dodge Roll" (DEFENCES.stardust - which of the two, asked where they
# differ); "For every Energy Charge or rank of Power Shot applied to that Attacking Maneuver, increase the Ki Point cost
# of this Maneuver by 1(bT)" (stardustKi). Won: avoided, and Reflect offered as a Parry's is.
stardust: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Counter against an Energy or Magic Attack: your Strike instead of your Dodge, 1(bT) more KP for each Energy Charge or
  rank of Power Shot on it; won, avoided, and Reflect as after a Parry.
text: >
  Stardust Barrier: You redirect an enemy’s attack away from you with the energy you project, protecting yourself from
  harm.
  –Ability Type: Technical
  –Prerequisites: Insight Score of 4+, Force Score of 8+
  –TP Cost: 15
  –KP Cost: 2(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Counter
  –Action Cost: 1 Counter Action
  –Minions: Free
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: If you are targeted by an Opponent’s Energy or Magic Attack, you may use your Physical or Energy Strike Roll
  instead of your Dodge Roll against that Attacking Maneuver’s Strike Roll. For every Energy Charge or rank of Power Shot
  applied to that Attacking Maneuver, increase the Ki Point cost of this Maneuver by 1(bT).

  If you win, you successfully avoid the Attacking Maneuver and may use the Reflect Modifier Maneuver as if this Maneuver
  was the Parry Maneuver.
